# FreeSail: the frigate's book for the Western Islands' passage (data/scenarios/
# azores.yaml; package 39e), Funchal Road to Angra Road. Short, as the brief has it: the
# points of the passage by the account, the landfall, the anchor. The reckoning is the
# log's and the noon sight's alone until the land is raised (no bearing is asked of a
# sea without marks); the points are wide, five miles and three, for an account days old.

# Across: a point north of St Mary's and St Michael's, then the channel between St
# Michael's and Terceira (every channel between the nine islands navigable, Tofiño 1789
# p. 211), then a point two miles south of the Cabras.
standing order "north of St Michaels": when the distance to 37 36 N 24 0 W is under 5 miles then shape a course for 38 24 N 26 24 W
standing order "between the islands": when the distance to 38 24 N 26 24 W is under 3 miles then shape a course for 38 36 N 27 6 W
standing order "past the Cabras": when the distance to 38 36 N 27 6 W is under 1 mile then shape a course for Angra Road; shorten sail
standing order "Angra": when the distance to Angra Road is under 1.5 miles and the depth of water by the chart is under 40 fathoms then come to an anchor

# The landfall: a bearing of the land when it is raised, and a fix when two marks serve.
standing order "landfall": at a landfall then take a bearing of the land
standing order "bearings": every glass, if the land is in sight then take a bearing of the land; take a fix
